ops off the decimal part instead of rounding. Floats can't hold amounts like 19.99 exactly, so `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.999\u2026`, which became 1998. Same thing with 0.29 (28.999\u2026 \u2192 28, so \u00d73 gave 84) and 4.35 (434.99\u2026 \u2192 434, which threw off the discount total).\n\n**The fix:** `to_cents` now converts with `Decimal(str(amount)) * 100` and rounds half-up. `str()` gives the short form of the float (`\"19.99\"`), so the multiply is exact. I used half-up rounding to match `apply_percent` in `ledger/discounts.py`. I left the discount code alone because it was already correct.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "provider_error": "Anthropic stream stalled while waiting for the next event", "read_calls": 8, "replies_ok": 5, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 32139, "requests_cache_write": 191906, "requests_cost_usd": 1.0006418, "requests_count": 7, "requests_input_uncached": 16, "requests_output": 1731, "reread": true, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-multistep:claude-opus-5-5:trial7", "run_seed": 1016, "sampling_observed": null, "schedule_index": 193, "score": 1.0, "started_at": "2026-10-20T02:26:19.574740+00:00", "subagent_resumed": false, "subagent_write_calls": 0, "success": true, "t_agent_s": 151.341, "t_checker_s": 0.426, "t_env_setup_s": 0.001, "task": "trig-omp-multistep", "task_calls": 0, "thinking_mode": "default", "thinking_sent": ["adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive", "adaptive"], "timeout_s": 840, "tmpdir_leaked_dirs": 0, "token_basis": "proxy_measured", "token_basis_main": "estimated", "token_basis_proxy": "proxy_measured", "tokens": 1747, "tokens_cache_read": 32139, "tokens_cache_write": 191906, "tokens_fresh": 1765, "tokens_input_uncached": 16, "tokens_main_cache_read": 61807, "tokens_main_cache_write": 193177, "tokens_main_calls": 8, "tokens_main_input_uncached": 18, "tok